+## Keys and roles
+
+Requests carry `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are stored in the data as
+`apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`. Roles:
+
+- `viewer`: GET only.
+- `cook`: also `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything.
+
+No key or an unknown key is `unauthorized` (401); a known key without
+permission is `forbidden` (403). Every non-GET request by a known key writes
+an audit entry `{ at, key, method, path, status }`; `GET /audit` (managers
+only) lists them newest first.
+
+## Routes
+
+See `README.md`; `GET /audit` is the audit log described above.
+
